{"pageProps":{"markdoc":{"content":[{"$$mdtype":"Tag","name":"p","attributes":{"class":"lead"},"children":["The ",{"$$mdtype":"Tag","name":"Link","attributes":{"href":"/docs/explorer"},"children":["plan explorer"]}," compares a policy with a current-state"," ","snapshot that you write or derive yourself. No pgroles command produces this"," ","file yet, and you must remove secrets from it by hand before importing or"," ","sharing it. "]},{"$$mdtype":"Tag","name":"h2","attributes":{"id":"where-the-format-is-defined"},"children":["Where the format is defined"]},{"$$mdtype":"Tag","name":"p","attributes":{},"children":["Snapshots use the ",{"$$mdtype":"Tag","name":"code","attributes":{},"children":["pgroles.explorer.v1"]}," request format. The"," ",{"$$mdtype":"Tag","name":"Link","attributes":{"href":"https://github.com/thepartly/pgroles/blob/main/crates/pgroles-wasm/README.md"},"children":["pgroles-wasm README"]}," ","is the only specification of it. This page does not restate the field list."," ","The analyzer decodes requests strictly and rejects unknown fields, so a typo"," ","fails loudly rather than being ignored."]},{"$$mdtype":"Tag","name":"p","attributes":{},"children":["The explorer accepts either a bare ",{"$$mdtype":"Tag","name":"code","attributes":{},"children":["current"]}," snapshot or a whole request"," ","envelope:"]},{"$$mdtype":"Tag","name":"Fence","attributes":{"language":"json"},"children":["{\n  \"schema_version\": \"pgroles.explorer.v1\",\n  \"pg_major_version\": 15,\n  \"authority_graph_complete\": false,\n  \"current\": {\n    \"roles\": { \"deploy\": { \"login\": true }, \"app_owner\": {} },\n    \"memberships\": [{ \"role\": \"app_owner\", \"member\": \"deploy\", \"inherit\": true, \"admin\": false }]\n  },\n  \"executor\": { \"role\": \"deploy\", \"createrole\": \"allowed\" }\n}\n"]},{"$$mdtype":"Tag","name":"p","attributes":{},"children":["The explorer uses ",{"$$mdtype":"Tag","name":"code","attributes":{},"children":["pg_major_version"]},", ",{"$$mdtype":"Tag","name":"code","attributes":{},"children":["authority_graph_complete"]},", and the"," ",{"$$mdtype":"Tag","name":"code","attributes":{},"children":["executor"]}," facts from an envelope, and shows ",{"$$mdtype":"Tag","name":"strong","attributes":{},"children":["From snapshot"]}," beside the"," ","PostgreSQL version when the envelope sets it. A bare snapshot keeps the version"," ","selected in the explorer and is treated as a complete authority graph. An"," ","envelope's ",{"$$mdtype":"Tag","name":"code","attributes":{},"children":["executor.superuser: true"]}," is kept even when ",{"$$mdtype":"Tag","name":"code","attributes":{},"children":["current.roles"]}," lists"," ","the executor without the flag, and the explorer shows ",{"$$mdtype":"Tag","name":"strong","attributes":{},"children":["Overrides snapshot"]}," ","beside the control; a snapshot ",{"$$mdtype":"Tag","name":"code","attributes":{},"children":["superuser: true"]}," cannot be unset. Typing a role"," ","the snapshot describes starts from that role's flag; tick the box to assert"," ","otherwise."]},{"$$mdtype":"Tag","name":"h2","attributes":{"id":"no-exporter-yet"},"children":["No exporter yet"]},{"$$mdtype":"Tag","name":"p","attributes":{},"children":["No CLI command writes an explorer snapshot. ",{"$$mdtype":"Tag","name":"code","attributes":{},"children":["pgroles inspect"]}," prints a"," ","summary, ",{"$$mdtype":"Tag","name":"code","attributes":{},"children":["pgroles generate"]}," writes a policy manifest, and"," ",{"$$mdtype":"Tag","name":"code","attributes":{},"children":["pgroles diff --review-out"]}," writes a"," ",{"$$mdtype":"Tag","name":"Link","attributes":{"href":"/docs/recorded-reviews"},"children":["recorded review"]}," (",{"$$mdtype":"Tag","name":"code","attributes":{},"children":["pgroles.review-artifact.v2"]},")."," ","A recorded review is a different format: the explorer displays it read-only"," ","and cannot replan it, because the export deliberately omits the inputs."]},{"$$mdtype":"Tag","name":"p","attributes":{},"children":["To explore a hypothetical change against a real database, build the snapshot"," ","yourself from catalog queries or from ",{"$$mdtype":"Tag","name":"code","attributes":{},"children":["pgroles inspect"]}," output. Include only"," ","the roles, schemas, grants, default privileges, and memberships that matter"," ","to the plan."]},{"$$mdtype":"Tag","name":"h2","attributes":{"id":"scrub-credentials-by-hand"},"children":["Scrub credentials by hand"]},{"$$mdtype":"Tag","name":"p","attributes":{},"children":["The analyzer rejects ",{"$$mdtype":"Tag","name":"code","attributes":{},"children":["password"]}," fields and password sources in desired YAML,"," ","but it cannot recognise a secret stored in a free-form string. Before you"," ","import or share a snapshot:"]},{"$$mdtype":"Tag","name":"ul","attributes":{},"children":[{"$$mdtype":"Tag","name":"li","attributes":{},"children":["Remove or replace every role ",{"$$mdtype":"Tag","name":"code","attributes":{},"children":["config"]}," value. ",{"$$mdtype":"Tag","name":"code","attributes":{},"children":["ALTER ROLE ... SET"]}," accepts"," ","arbitrary strings, and teams sometimes store connection strings, API keys,"," ","or tokens there."]},{"$$mdtype":"Tag","name":"li","attributes":{},"children":["Remove or replace every role ",{"$$mdtype":"Tag","name":"code","attributes":{},"children":["comment"]},". Comments are free text and can"," ","contain credentials or internal notes."]},{"$$mdtype":"Tag","name":"li","attributes":{},"children":["Review role, schema, and object names, and the executor role. They are"," ","kept verbatim and can reveal customer or system names."]}]},{"$$mdtype":"Tag","name":"p","attributes":{},"children":["The browser does not upload, store, or put the snapshot in the URL, but a"," ","file you share with someone else takes its contents with it."]},{"$$mdtype":"Tag","name":"h2","attributes":{"id":"postgre-sql-version"},"children":["PostgreSQL version"]},{"$$mdtype":"Tag","name":"p","attributes":{},"children":[{"$$mdtype":"Tag","name":"code","attributes":{},"children":["pg_major_version"]}," is the target server's major version. It defaults to 16"," ","when omitted. The explorer offers 15 to 18; the analyzer accepts 12 to 20 and"," ","rejects anything else. The results header shows the version the analyzer"," ","used."]},{"$$mdtype":"Tag","name":"p","attributes":{},"children":["The version changes the authority needed to grant or revoke role membership"," ","(adding a member, or removing one without ",{"$$mdtype":"Tag","name":"code","attributes":{},"children":["GRANTED BY"]},"), and what a membership"," ","proves about ",{"$$mdtype":"Tag","name":"code","attributes":{},"children":["SET ROLE"]},":"]},{"$$mdtype":"Tag","name":"ul","attributes":{},"children":[{"$$mdtype":"Tag","name":"li","attributes":{},"children":[{"$$mdtype":"Tag","name":"strong","attributes":{},"children":["Before PostgreSQL 16"]},", an executor with ",{"$$mdtype":"Tag","name":"code","attributes":{},"children":["CREATEROLE"]}," may grant and"," ","revoke membership in any non-superuser role without ",{"$$mdtype":"Tag","name":"code","attributes":{},"children":["ADMIN OPTION"]},". When"," ",{"$$mdtype":"Tag","name":"code","attributes":{},"children":["CREATEROLE"]}," is unknown and ",{"$$mdtype":"Tag","name":"code","attributes":{},"children":["ADMIN OPTION"]}," is not proven, the explorer"," ","reports the authority as not proven."]},{"$$mdtype":"Tag","name":"li","attributes":{},"children":[{"$$mdtype":"Tag","name":"strong","attributes":{},"children":["From PostgreSQL 16"]},", the executor needs ",{"$$mdtype":"Tag","name":"code","attributes":{},"children":["ADMIN OPTION"]}," on the granted"," ","role, directly or through a role whose privileges it inherits. ",{"$$mdtype":"Tag","name":"code","attributes":{},"children":["CREATEROLE"]}," ","alone is not enough."]},{"$$mdtype":"Tag","name":"li","attributes":{},"children":[{"$$mdtype":"Tag","name":"strong","attributes":{},"children":["In every version"]},", only a superuser executor can grant or revoke"," ","membership in a superuser role (",{"$$mdtype":"Tag","name":"code","attributes":{},"children":["superuser_required"]},")."]},{"$$mdtype":"Tag","name":"li","attributes":{},"children":[{"$$mdtype":"Tag","name":"strong","attributes":{},"children":["Before PostgreSQL 16"]},", there is no per-membership ",{"$$mdtype":"Tag","name":"code","attributes":{},"children":["SET"]}," option, so every"," ","membership in the snapshot, in executor facts, or added by the plan proves"," ",{"$$mdtype":"Tag","name":"code","attributes":{},"children":["SET ROLE"]}," to the granted role. ",{"$$mdtype":"Tag","name":"strong","attributes":{},"children":["From PostgreSQL 16"]},", a membership without"," ","a ",{"$$mdtype":"Tag","name":"code","attributes":{},"children":["set_role"]}," executor fact is a possible path but not a proven one."]}]},{"$$mdtype":"Tag","name":"p","attributes":{},"children":["It does not change how the ",{"$$mdtype":"Tag","name":"code","attributes":{},"children":["INHERIT"]}," option is modelled, grantor attribution,"," ","or which changes are planned."]},{"$$mdtype":"Tag","name":"p","attributes":{},"children":[{"$$mdtype":"Tag","name":"code","attributes":{},"children":["executor.createrole"]}," (",{"$$mdtype":"Tag","name":"code","attributes":{},"children":["allowed"]},", ",{"$$mdtype":"Tag","name":"code","attributes":{},"children":["denied"]},", or ",{"$$mdtype":"Tag","name":"code","attributes":{},"children":["unknown"]},", the default) is"," ","consulted only below PostgreSQL 16. ",{"$$mdtype":"Tag","name":"code","attributes":{},"children":["allowed"]}," or ",{"$$mdtype":"Tag","name":"code","attributes":{},"children":["denied"]}," overrides the"," ","snapshot; ",{"$$mdtype":"Tag","name":"code","attributes":{},"children":["unknown"]}," uses the ",{"$$mdtype":"Tag","name":"code","attributes":{},"children":["createrole"]}," attribute of the executor's own"," ","role when the snapshot includes it. The ",{"$$mdtype":"Tag","name":"strong","attributes":{},"children":["Executor CREATEROLE"]}," control in the"," ","explorer sets this fact."]},{"$$mdtype":"Tag","name":"h2","attributes":{"id":"authority-graph-completeness"},"children":["Authority graph completeness"]},{"$$mdtype":"Tag","name":"p","attributes":{},"children":[{"$$mdtype":"Tag","name":"code","attributes":{},"children":["authority_graph_complete"]}," defaults to ",{"$$mdtype":"Tag","name":"code","attributes":{},"children":["true"]},". It states whether the snapshot"," ","and executor facts list every role and membership that could give the"," ","executor authority."]},{"$$mdtype":"Tag","name":"ul","attributes":{},"children":[{"$$mdtype":"Tag","name":"li","attributes":{},"children":[{"$$mdtype":"Tag","name":"strong","attributes":{},"children":["Complete"]}," (",{"$$mdtype":"Tag","name":"code","attributes":{},"children":["true"]},"): a missing path proves the executor lacks that"," ","authority. Roles without a path are ",{"$$mdtype":"Tag","name":"code","attributes":{},"children":["unreachable"]},", and missing grantor,"," ","owner, ",{"$$mdtype":"Tag","name":"code","attributes":{},"children":["ADMIN OPTION"]},", or ",{"$$mdtype":"Tag","name":"code","attributes":{},"children":["CREATEROLE"]}," authority is a"," ",{"$$mdtype":"Tag","name":"code","attributes":{},"children":["required_role_unavailable"]}," error."]},{"$$mdtype":"Tag","name":"li","attributes":{},"children":[{"$$mdtype":"Tag","name":"strong","attributes":{},"children":["Partial"]}," (",{"$$mdtype":"Tag","name":"code","attributes":{},"children":["false"]},"): a missing path is only unproven. Those roles are"," ",{"$$mdtype":"Tag","name":"code","attributes":{},"children":["unknown"]},", the same gaps are ",{"$$mdtype":"Tag","name":"code","attributes":{},"children":["required_role_reachability_unknown"]}," warnings"," ","that need a database preflight, and losing a path that was only possible is"," ","not reported as a disconnection. Losing a proven path is still reported as"," ",{"$$mdtype":"Tag","name":"code","attributes":{},"children":["executor_loses_access"]},"."]}]},{"$$mdtype":"Tag","name":"p","attributes":{},"children":["Set it to ",{"$$mdtype":"Tag","name":"code","attributes":{},"children":["false"]}," when the snapshot covers only the managed roles. Native"," ","recorded reviews always use ",{"$$mdtype":"Tag","name":"code","attributes":{},"children":["false"]},", because inspection is scoped to the"," ","policy. The explorer sends ",{"$$mdtype":"Tag","name":"code","attributes":{},"children":["true"]}," unless a bundled scenario variant or an"," ","imported envelope sets it to ",{"$$mdtype":"Tag","name":"code","attributes":{},"children":["false"]},", and shows the setting under"," ",{"$$mdtype":"Tag","name":"strong","attributes":{},"children":["Current snapshot"]},"."]}],"frontmatter":{"title":"Explorer snapshots","description":"Prepare a current-state snapshot for the browser plan explorer, scrub it by hand, and understand how the PostgreSQL version and authority-graph settings change the results."},"file":{"path":"/docs/explorer-snapshots.md"}}},"__N_SSG":true}